[{"article": {"id": "04d6500e-a311-49f7-a786-274fcc7918b9", "title": "‘I suggested maybe a lighter touch’: William Shatner on Star Trek at 60", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/sep/08/star-trek-at-60-william-shatner", "summary": "The actor and others involved with the phenomenon speak about the legacy and progressivism of a much-loved science fiction TV series as it reaches an important milestone‘The mystery of time,” musesWilliam Shatner, and for a moment we are back on the bridge of the Starship Enterprise listening to one of Captain Kirk’s philosophical tag-line speeches. “Not just the passage of time and our perception of it, but what is time? What does 60 years mean? It really is meaningless, isn’t it, 60 years, in terms of what time is? On the other hand, Dolly Parton just died. It brings up the whole concept of the passage of time and what that means.”In an episode called The City on the Edge of Forever, Shatner’s Kirk travelled back in time and fell in love with a pacifist (Joan Collins) only to discover that she must die to prevent Nazi Germany winning the second world war. Such ethical quandaries help explain why Star Trek willcelebrate its 60th anniversaryon 8 September not just as a force in US c...", "published_at": "2026-09-08T09:00:55+00:00", "image_url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/6e6cddfec7acf0829a12291f1f1cc3a907df27d3/0_263_2682_2145/master/2682.jpg?width=1200&height=630&quality=85&auto=format&fit=crop&precrop=40:21,offset-x50,offset-y0&overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&overlay-width=100p&overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdGctZGVmYXVsdC5wbmc&enable=upscale&s=1fc32cd724d847063103ce2dffed68d4", "source": {"name": "The Guardian Australia", "tier": "international", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/au"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 50, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 6, "confidence": 0.7, "rationale": {"framing": {"connotation_score": 0.0, "keyword_emphasis_score": 0.0, "omissi